   - "The VM desktop path needs xdotool, a screenshot tool (scrot, maim or ImageMagick import), the AT-SPI bus and python3-gi on the VM. Without them those calls fail and the agent reports it; setup.sh warns about what is missing."
   - "A default som capture skips the screenshot request when snapshot geometry establishes 35% named-control coverage; older apps without geometry still require a screenshot to check it and may omit it from the model. Use mode vision to request it explicitly, or mode ax for an element-only capture. When a screenshot is omitted, coordinate= and element bounds are screen pixels."
   - "Mac and Windows action replies update the held element list without shifting surviving numbers. On Linux, capture again before acting by number after a tree change; cut replies do not prove an unseen control is gone. A timeout or hung app can leave the action's outcome uncertain: capture before retrying."
-  - "This release changes provider code: focus_app launches a named app, or opens a document or folder by absolute path in its app on the user's computer (needs Alan's Workspace 0.21.9 with computer-open-v1; app bundles, executables, scripts and off-limits apps are refused). It binds the window showing the opened item. When an action lands on an unfocused window it returns that error and tells the model to ask for a raise explicitly (focus_app with raise_window=true, or delivery_mode='foreground'), which Hermes approves under its foreground scopes; the provider never raises on its own. It follows the focused window after an app shortcut, and passes the app's step notes to the model. Older apps refuse path opens and keep the earlier behavior."
+  - "focus_app launches a named app, or opens a document or folder by absolute path in its app on the user's computer (needs Alan's Workspace 0.21.9 with computer-open-v1; app bundles, executables, scripts and off-limits apps are refused). It binds the window showing the opened item. When an action lands on an unfocused window it returns that error and tells the model to ask for a raise explicitly (focus_app with raise_window=true, or delivery_mode='foreground'), which Hermes approves under its foreground scopes; the provider never raises on its own. It follows the focused window after an app shortcut, and passes the app's step notes to the model. Older apps refuse path opens and keep the earlier behavior."
   - "Admission validation passes with a private-import warning: __init__.py uses tools.mcp_tool_config._resolve_stdio_command to resolve the router launcher; this internal helper may change across Hermes releases."
+  - "When the Mac reports desktop_busy (another agent holds the desktop), launch, menu and action calls are resent for up to 30 s of waiting, following the host's retry-after hint or every 2 s, then fail with desktop_busy naming the holder. Hermes does not ask for approval again on a resend; the host refused the call before running it."
