+version: "0.2.0"
+requires_hermes: ">=0.21.7"
+description: "Dry-run mode for Hermes Agent. With /ghost on, file writes, patches, deletes and terminal commands are redirected into a throwaway copy of the working folder, and network-touching tools and commands are blocked. Review the diff in the system browser (hermes ghost ui; the Desktop pane only opens that page), then optionally run one configured Verify command in the ghost (Pass/Fail banner; Apply stays human), then apply selected paths or discard. Commands: /ghost on|off|status|verify; hermes ghost diff|apply|discard|ui|verify. Disclosure — copies the working folder into a temp sandbox (reflink, then copy; never a hard link) and runs the agent's terminal commands on the host with the working directory set to that copy; only literal absolute paths under the real folder are rewritten, so a command naming ~, $HOME or another absolute path still acts on the real disk, and MCP or other plugin tools are not redirected; Ghost Mode is process-wide, so in a gateway it covers every chat in that process; writes session state under the Hermes home from hermes_constants.get_hermes_home() (then HERMES_HOME, then ~/.hermes), in ghost-run/; \"apply\" writes the chosen changes back to the real folder only after a person presses Apply or runs /ghost apply, and that copy does not pass through Hermes' file-write denylist; /ghost apply and hermes ghost apply with no paths apply every current change and can copy a named path that is in the ghost tree even if it is not in the diff; the review page never auto-ticks HIGH-risk files and asks to confirm any it names; hermes ghost ui binds 127.0.0.1 only, checks Host, requires a per-session token sent in the X-Ghost-Run-Token header (query-string tokens are ignored), sends no CORS headers, and POST /api/apply accepts only a non-empty list of paths that are all in the current diff; Verify runs one command taken from GHOST_RUN_TEST or the project's .ghost-run-test on the host inside the ghost copy, only after you approve that project and exact command, with provider keys stripped from its environment; opt-in outbound only: with GHOST_RUN_AI=1, pending diffs go to your Hermes provider through ctx.llm.complete, or, if that is unavailable, to openrouter.ai using OPENROUTER_API_KEY read only via agent.secret_scope.get_secret; off by default, no credentials stored by the plugin, no telemetry."
