+name: hermes-continuum
+repo: https://github.com/mohamad-shafeez/hermes-continuum
+sha: 5da4774fb7453447aeae61f3d3288dbbf20d914c
+version: "0.3.0"
+description: "An integrated nine-system plugin for Hermes Agent that provides task continuity, review-first episodic memory, environment reality checks, evidence tracking, goal integrity, trust-aware tool policies, impact previews, retry-loop protection, and verified workflow distillation. Its systems share an append-only SQLite Event Spine and a Continuum Console for Hermes Desktop. Includes 12 tools, 11 lifecycle hooks, checkpoint export, and a review-first approach to generated artifacts. Live verification and test coverage are documented in the repository; not every capability has been verified in a live host workflow. Disclosure — Records every tool call, approval prompt/response and session event (with redacted argument previews) in a local plugin database; its pre_tool_call policy can block tool calls or escalate them to Hermes' approval prompt, labels web/browser results as untrusted, injects recalled memory facts (including unreviewed candidates) and an auto-built task charter into each turn, and its model-callable continuum_forge tool can register new plugin skills and automation blueprints distilled from session traces when called with confirm: true."
+maintainer: mohamad-shafeez
+tier: community
+category: desktop
+requires_hermes: ">=0.22.2"
+docs_url: https://github.com/mohamad-shafeez/hermes-continuum#readme
+readme: true
