+description: "Holdings is a Hermes Desktop plugin that shows your crypto wallet and exchange balances in one place. You can review activity against the original records and export records with a note on what each source covers. Ask Holdings answers questions with your Hermes model and checks every cited number against your records. It is read-only and never signs transactions or moves funds. The demo uses fictional records and needs no keys. Disclosure — crypto portfolio viewer, read-only (no signing, transfers or trades). Sends the wallet addresses you add and your read-only exchange API keys (stored through Hermes secrets) to their own vendors: Kraken, Binance, Bybit, Etherscan, Zerion, GoPlus, public RPCs (PublicNode, dRPC, MEV Blocker, Solana mainnet), DefiLlama and GeckoTerminal. Saved wallet and exchange records go to your active model only after you enable `share_private_chat_tools` (off by default). Weekly briefing and alert watch cron jobs are opt-in templates."
