+# Submission entry pinned to published immutable source.
+name: look
+title: Look
+repo: https://github.com/SilentHacks/look
+sha: "7c01a94aa651adedaf27e5216598c6deef293050"
+version: "0.1.0"
+requires_hermes: ">=0.23.1"
+description: "Ask about pages and use guarded Chrome actions. Apple Silicon macOS beta with broad debugger access and optional local voice and eyes. Disclosure — Look runs its own Chrome profile (~/.cache/look/chrome-profile) on a loopback DevTools port and sends your questions and captured page evidence to your configured model. Model-requested navigation and link clicks refuse private, loopback and metadata hosts only before navigating (redirects and DNS rebinding are not contained; the owner setting allow_private_network turns the check off). `/look actions allow-all` skips Look's own action review for the bound conversation. When TYPESAFE_API_KEY is set (early_highlight is on by default), your spoken question and pointer structure, plus page text if highlight_include_page_text is on, go to api.typesafe.ai. Setup downloads checksum-pinned NVIDIA NeMo-Speech native libraries, Hugging Face speech models and MediaPipe WASM into ~/Library/Caches/Look and ~/.cache/look."
+maintainer: SilentHacks
+tier: community
+category: web
+docs_url: https://github.com/SilentHacks/look
+readme: true
+screenshots:
+  - https://raw.githubusercontent.com/SilentHacks/look/7c01a94aa651adedaf27e5216598c6deef293050/docs/catalog/screenshots/01-typed-input.png
+  - https://raw.githubusercontent.com/SilentHacks/look/7c01a94aa651adedaf27e5216598c6deef293050/docs/catalog/screenshots/02-scripted-answer.png
+  - https://raw.githubusercontent.com/SilentHacks/look/7c01a94aa651adedaf27e5216598c6deef293050/docs/catalog/screenshots/03-followup-input.png
+  - https://raw.githubusercontent.com/SilentHacks/look/7c01a94aa651adedaf27e5216598c6deef293050/docs/catalog/screenshots/04-followup-answer.png
+  - https://raw.githubusercontent.com/SilentHacks/look/7c01a94aa651adedaf27e5216598c6deef293050/docs/catalog/screenshots/05-protected-action-review.png
+  - https://raw.githubusercontent.com/SilentHacks/look/7c01a94aa651adedaf27e5216598c6deef293050/docs/catalog/screenshots/06-extension-consent.png
+platforms:
+  - macos
+known_issues:
+  - "Requires Apple Silicon, native arm64 Python 3.11–3.14, Chrome, one display and an in-process local Hermes session with input permission."
+  - "Eye tracking is experimental. Real-camera accuracy and screen-reader compatibility are unverified. English-first voice and UI."
+  - "Questions and page evidence reach the configured model. Optional TypeSafe scope requests can add costs."
+  - "Explicit allow-all skips Look action review for requested actions. Chrome sign-ins, model caches, calibration and Hermes/provider history survive plugin removal."
+  - "Gallery shows fixture-backed UI captured before v3 integration, with scripted answers and no provider inference. Not native Chrome consent or a fresh install."
