+name: offgrid
+repo: https://github.com/emmaGH1/hermes-offgrid
+sha: "5332d4d62ea75ff68011059d73a6562e79f08b86"
+version: "1.0.0"
+title: Offgrid
+image: https://raw.githubusercontent.com/emmaGH1/hermes-offgrid/5332d4d62ea75ff68011059d73a6562e79f08b86/assets/logo.png
+description: "Chat with your Hermes agent by plain SMS, with no mobile data, through Africa's Talking, plus a USSD menu as a fallback for basic phones. Texts become normal Hermes messages on the offgrid platform, one conversation per phone number, and replies come back as a single SMS (Markdown and emoji stripped, capped at five billed segments). A safe subset of gateway commands works by text: NEW, SESSIONS, RESUME <n>, MODEL, STATUS, HELP and /retry, /stop, /title; every other slash command is refused by default. Disclosure — every question and every reply is sent through Africa's Talking and the mobile network as SMS, in plain text, and each outbound SMS segment (up to five per reply) is billed to the operator's Africa's Talking account (incoming SMS and USSD sessions may also be billed). Requires an Africa's Talking API key, a callback secret and an explicit allowlist of phone numbers; the callback must be reachable over public HTTPS (the listener binds 127.0.0.1:8080 by default, so a tunnel or reverse proxy is needed). SMS sender numbers can be spoofed: a spoofed text from an allowlisted number gets a normal agent turn with this profile's tools and memory (the reply goes to the real number), while commands that change config, approve tools or reveal other sessions are blocked and dangerous commands time out unapproved. Verified in the Africa's Talking sandbox only, not on a live carrier. Uses its own platform name and OFFGRID_* settings, so it installs alongside ussd-platform."
+maintainer: emmaGH1
+tier: community
+category: platform
+requires_hermes: ">=0.23.1"
+docs_url: https://github.com/emmaGH1/hermes-offgrid#readme
+readme: true
+platforms: [linux]
+capabilities:
+  provides_tools: []
+  provides_hooks: []
+  provides_middleware: []
+  requires_env: [AT_API_KEY, AT_USERNAME, OFFGRID_CALLBACK_SECRET, OFFGRID_ALLOWED_USERS]
+known_issues:
+  - "Sandbox only: not yet tested on a live carrier or physical handset."
+  - "Questions are dispatched by one worker from an in-memory queue, so one slow answer delays others and a crash can lose queued questions."
+  - "Texts over the per-phone rate limit or over 500 characters are dropped without a reply."
+  - "An SMS user cannot answer a dangerous-command approval prompt; it times out and the action is blocked."
