+name: pinpoint
+repo: https://github.com/stupidburgers/pinpoint
+sha: "06b911e1c66908ebf340c6cb981028bc45b89c73"
+subdir: ""
+description: "Audit mode and Design mode for the live page in Hermes Desktop's Browser pane. Measure it with in-page audits (contrast, tap targets, alt/labels, overflow, small text), pin findings on the real elements, point at any element to inspect its live box model, typography, layout and contrast, send a pin or an instruction to the agent, and re-audit to get a score delta, a pasteable receipt and a per-pin outcome: fixed (no longer reported and the same element signature is still present; not a re-measurement), gone (element signature missing, never counted as a fix) or not rechecked (unverifiable, stays open). Disclosure - Pinpoint's desktop half runs its own audit script inside the web page open in Hermes Desktop's Browser pane, only after you allow it for that site (Desktop's per-origin consent dialog; revocable under Capabilities > Plugins). The script reads computed styles, layout, the page's visible text, and the values of the attributes id, name, href, src, alt and aria-label (plus title and placeholder when it works out an element's accessible name); it contains no cookie access and does not read form-field values, and it draws an overlay. Findings (CSS selectors, short element labels that can contain page text, measured values) are stored locally in a SQLite file under the plugin-data folder (`pinpoint/data.db`; at most 20 pages, 200 pins and 50 audits per page; entries older than 7 days are pruned). They are sent to the model only when the agent calls `pinpoint_audit`/`pinpoint_pins` or when you click Fix, Fix all high or Send in the Desktop pane (or its command-palette action); an event raised by the page itself never sends a chat turn. Pinpoint also adds a short hint to the system prompt that names its two tools. The desktop half polls the page every 0.5-1 s while pins are shown (via `executeJavaScript`) and re-audits automatically after page changes (switch off in the pane). `pinpoint_audit` blocks up to 90 s waiting for the Desktop (configurable) and returns `desktop_unavailable` when no Desktop window answers, including under cron. No network calls, no subprocesses, no shell, no credentials, no telemetry, no files written outside plugin-data; it never edits your source (the agent does, under normal approvals). Limits: verified on Windows 11 with Hermes 0.22.7 only (macOS and Linux are untested). Results are a limited heuristic audit, not WCAG certification, and fixed / gone describe what this engine observed, not a guarantee about your page. Disclosure — Pinpoint's desktop half runs its own audit script inside the web page open in Hermes Desktop's Browser pane, only after you allow it for that site (Desktop's per-origin consent dialog; revocable under Capabilities > Plugins); the script reads computed styles, layout, the page's visible text and the attributes id, name, href, src, alt, aria-label, title and placeholder, not form-field values or cookies, and draws an overlay. Findings (CSS selectors, short element labels that can contain page text, measured values) are stored in a local SQLite file under the plugin-data folder (pinpoint/data.db; at most 20 pages, 200 pins and 50 audits per page, pruned after 7 days) and reach the model only when the agent calls pinpoint_audit/pinpoint_pins (pinpoint_audit can also return the live box model of a model-chosen CSS selector) or when you click Fix, Fix all high or Send in the Pinpoint pane or its palette actions; an event raised by the page never sends a chat turn. The plugin adds a short hint to the system prompt naming its two tools. The desktop half polls the page every 0.5-1 s while pins are shown (via executeJavaScript) and re-audits automatically after page changes (switch off in the pane). pinpoint_audit blocks up to 90 s waiting for the Desktop (configurable) and returns desktop_unavailable when no Desktop window answers, including under cron. No network calls, subprocesses, shell, credentials or telemetry, and no files written outside plugin-data; it never edits your source (the agent does, under normal approvals). Verified on Windows 11 only; results
+  are a heuristic audit, not WCAG certification."
+maintainer: stupidburgers
+tier: community
+category: desktop
+requires_hermes: ">=0.22.7"
+version: "0.1.0"
+image: "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/stupidburgers/pinpoint/d97399a6ec82391e736eccdfd0b75f00ef7c7eef/docs/banner.png"
+screenshots:
+  - "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/stupidburgers/pinpoint/d97399a6ec82391e736eccdfd0b75f00ef7c7eef/docs/screenshots/01-pins.png"
+  - "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/stupidburgers/pinpoint/d97399a6ec82391e736eccdfd0b75f00ef7c7eef/docs/screenshots/02-pin-card.png"
+  - "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/stupidburgers/pinpoint/d97399a6ec82391e736eccdfd0b75f00ef7c7eef/docs/screenshots/03-after-fix.png"
